IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `qwhs-dates`

-- Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Qld) -- the rules a worker meets when hurt at work, put at risk, or treated badly for
-- raising safety: who is a worker (ss 5, 7); the maximum penalties the person responsible faces (ss 31-34, 34C-34E);
-- incident notification (Part 3, ss 35-39); the right to cease unsafe work (Part 5 Div 6, ss 83-88); discriminatory,
-- coercive and misleading conduct, and the civil claim for it (Part 6, the whole Part, ss 104-115); compensation for
-- an inspector's entry powers (s 184); review of decisions (Part 12, ss 223-229EA, schedule 2A); asking for a
-- prosecution and the limitation period for one (ss 231, 232); civil liability (s 267); no contracting out and no levy
-- on workers (ss 272, 273).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in qwhs-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule.
-- Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("means", "if", "only if", "may
-- only be made if", "must not", "does not", "can not", a period the Act fixes that has run); or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. Judgments
-- the Act leaves to someone else ("reasonable concern", "reasonably considers", "just", "substantial reason", "the
-- conduct was reasonable in the circumstances", "unreasonably failed") are inputs: the answer is conditional on them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) The State of Queensland,
-- CC BY 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See
-- NOTES.md.

§ `Work Health and Safety Act 2011`

§§ `ss 5, 7 -- worker and person conducting a business or undertaking`

-- s 5(1), (4), (7), (8): a person conducts a business or undertaking alone or with others, for profit or not; not "to
-- the extent that the person is engaged solely as a worker in, or as an officer of" it; "A volunteer association does
-- not conduct a business or undertaking" (a group of volunteers none of whom employs anyone to carry out work for it).
-- s 5(6) lets a regulation say otherwise; no regulation is deposited, so it is asked as a fact.
-- "does not" -- a flat negative: JUST FALSE. Otherwise whether there is a "business or undertaking" is a borrowed
-- term, asked as a fact; NOTHING-kind: leaves a term undefined, where the person says there is none.
GIVEN `there is a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is a volunteer association` IS A BOOLEAN, `a regulation says it is not one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5 -- it is a person conducting a business or undertaking` `there is a business or undertaking` `it is a volunteer association` `a regulation says it is not one` MEANS
    IF `it is a volunteer association` OR `a regulation says it is not one`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `there is a business or undertaking`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

-- s 7(1): "A person is a worker if the person carries out work in any capacity for a person conducting a business or
-- undertaking, including work as" an employee, contractor, subcontractor, their employee, labour hire employee,
-- outworker, apprentice or trainee, work experience student, volunteer, or a prescribed class. The list after
-- "including" only illustrates; the test is the "if". s 7(2): a police officer is a worker, at work while on duty or
-- lawfully performing police functions. s 7(3): the individual who conducts the business is also a worker if they carry
-- out work in it.
-- "if" -- JUST FALSE when the work is not for a person conducting a business or undertaking (and not a police officer).
GIVEN `I carry out work for it` IS A BOOLEAN, `it conducts a business or undertaking` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, `I am a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7 -- I am a worker` `I carry out work for it` `it conducts a business or undertaking` `I am a police officer` MEANS
    IF `I am a police officer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF NOT `I carry out work for it`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE CONSIDER `it conducts a business or undertaking`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
              -- NOTHING-kind: leaves a term undefined (whether there is a business or undertaking at all).
              OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `ss 31-34, 34A-34E -- what the person responsible can face`

DECLARE `Offence` IS ONE OF
    `category 1 -- reckless or negligent conduct exposing me to a risk of death or serious injury or illness`
    `category 2 -- failure to comply with a duty that exposed me to a risk of death or serious injury or illness`
    `category 3 -- failure to comply with a health and safety duty`
    `industrial manslaughter by the person conducting the business or undertaking`
    `industrial manslaughter by a senior officer`
    `discriminatory, coercive or misleading conduct (ss 104, 107, 108, 109)`

DECLARE `Offender` IS ONE OF
    `an individual, not as a person conducting a business or undertaking or as its officer`
    `an individual, as a person conducting a business or undertaking or as its officer`
    `a body corporate`

-- The maximum penalty: penalty units (0 if none is stated) and years of imprisonment (0 if none is stated). The value of a
-- penalty unit is set under the Penalties and Sentences Act 1992 and its regulation (not deposited), so units are given.
DECLARE `Maximum penalty` HAS
    `penalty units` IS A NUMBER
    `years of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Penalty answer` IS ONE OF
    `the maximum penalty is` HAS `the penalty` IS A `Maximum penalty`
    `no offence by this person (a volunteer)`
    `not an offence this kind of offender can commit`

GIVEN u IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Penalty answer`
`at most` u `units or` y `years` MEANS `the maximum penalty is` (`Maximum penalty` WITH `penalty units` IS u, `years of imprisonment` IS y)

-- s 31(1), s 32, s 33, s 34C(1), s 34D(1), ss 104, 107, 108, 109: the maximum penalties as printed. s 34(1): "A volunteer
-- does not commit an offence under this division for a failure to comply with a health and safety duty, except a duty
-- under section 28 or 29" (the duties of workers and of other persons at a workplace); s 34B(1): "A volunteer does not
-- commit an offence under this part" (Part 2A). s 34D is an offence of a senior officer, an individual, so a body
-- corporate cannot commit it. The ss 104-109 offences are 1,000 penalty units for anyone.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`, `the offender` IS AN `Offender`, `the offender is a volunteer` IS A BOOLEAN, `the duty is a worker's or other person's duty (ss 28, 29)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Penalty answer`
`ss 31-34D, 104-109 -- the maximum penalty` `the offence` `the offender` `the offender is a volunteer` `the duty is a worker's or other person's duty (ss 28, 29)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `discriminatory, coercive or misleading conduct (ss 104, 107, 108, 109)` THEN `at most` 1000 `units or` 0 `years`
    WHEN `industrial manslaughter by the person conducting the business or undertaking` THEN
        IF `the offender is a volunteer`
        THEN `no offence by this person (a volunteer)`
        ELSE CONSIDER `the offender`
             WHEN `a body corporate` THEN `at most` 100000 `units or` 0 `years`
             OTHERWISE `at most` 0 `units or` 20 `years`
    WHEN `industrial manslaughter by a senior officer` THEN
        IF `the offender is a volunteer`
        THEN `no offence by this person (a volunteer)`
        ELSE CONSIDER `the offender`
             WHEN `a body corporate` THEN `not an offence this kind of offender can commit`
             OTHERWISE `at most` 0 `units or` 20 `years`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the offender is a volunteer` AND (NOT `the duty is a worker's or other person's duty (ss 28, 29)`)
        THEN `no offence by this person (a volunteer)`
        ELSE CONSIDER `the offence`
             WHEN `category 1 -- reckless or negligent conduct exposing me to a risk of death or serious injury or illness` THEN
                 CONSIDER `the offender`
                 WHEN `a body corporate` THEN `at most` 30000 `units or` 0 `years`
                 WHEN `an individual, as a person conducting a business or undertaking or as its officer` THEN `at most` 6000 `units or` 5 `years`
                 OTHERWISE `at most` 3000 `units or` 5 `years`
             WHEN `category 2 -- failure to comply with a duty that exposed me to a risk of death or serious injury or illness` THEN
                 CONSIDER `the offender`
                 WHEN `a body corporate` THEN `at most` 15000 `units or` 0 `years`
                 WHEN `an individual, as a person conducting a business or undertaking or as its officer` THEN `at most` 3000 `units or` 0 `years`
                 OTHERWISE `at most` 1500 `units or` 0 `years`
             OTHERWISE
                 CONSIDER `the offender`
                 WHEN `a body corporate` THEN `at most` 5000 `units or` 0 `years`
                 WHEN `an individual, as a person conducting a business or undertaking or as its officer` THEN `at most` 1000 `units or` 0 `years`
                 OTHERWISE `at most` 500 `units or` 0 `years`

§§ `Part 3 -- incident notification`

-- s 36(b): the kinds of immediate treatment.
DECLARE `Immediate treatment` IS ONE OF
    `amputation of any part of the body`
    `a serious head injury`
    `a serious eye injury`
    `a serious burn`
    `separation of skin from underlying tissue (degloving or scalping)`
    `a spinal injury`
    `the loss of a bodily function`
    `serious lacerations`
    `none of these`

-- s 36: "serious injury or illness of a person means an injury or illness requiring the person to have-- (a) immediate
-- treatment as an in-patient in a hospital; or (b) immediate treatment for-- [the list]; or (c) medical treatment within
-- 48 hours of exposure to a substance; and includes any other injury or illness prescribed under a regulation but does
-- not include an illness or injury of a prescribed kind." No regulation is deposited: the prescribed inclusions and
-- exclusions are asked as facts.
-- "means" -- JUST FALSE when no limb holds; "does not include" -- JUST FALSE for a prescribed exclusion.
GIVEN `in-patient` IS A BOOLEAN, `treatment` IS AN `Immediate treatment`, `48 hours` IS A BOOLEAN, `prescribed as included` IS A BOOLEAN, `prescribed as excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36 -- serious injury or illness` `in-patient` `treatment` `48 hours` `prescribed as included` `prescribed as excluded` MEANS
    IF `prescribed as excluded`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `in-patient` OR `a listed treatment` OR `48 hours` OR `prescribed as included`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `a listed treatment` MEANS
            CONSIDER `treatment`
            WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 37(a)-(k): what the immediate or imminent exposure was to.
DECLARE `Exposure` IS ONE OF
    `an uncontrolled escape, spillage or leakage of a substance`
    `an uncontrolled implosion, explosion or fire`
    `an uncontrolled escape of gas or steam`
    `an uncontrolled escape of a pressurised substance`
    `electric shock`
    `the fall or release from a height of any plant, substance or thing`
    `the collapse, overturning, failure or malfunction of, or damage to, plant required to be authorised`
    `the collapse or partial collapse of a structure`
    `the collapse or failure of an excavation or its shoring`
    `the inrush of water, mud or gas in workings, an underground excavation or tunnel`
    `the interruption of the main ventilation in an underground excavation or tunnel`
    `another event prescribed under a regulation`
    `none of these`

-- s 37: "a dangerous incident means an incident in relation to a workplace that exposes a worker or any other person to
-- a serious risk to a person's health or safety emanating from an immediate or imminent exposure to" (a)-(l), "but does
-- not include an incident of a prescribed kind". "means" -- JUST FALSE when it fails.
GIVEN `at a workplace` IS A BOOLEAN, `serious risk` IS A BOOLEAN, `the exposure` IS AN `Exposure`, `prescribed as excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37 -- dangerous incident` `at a workplace` `serious risk` `the exposure` `prescribed as excluded` MEANS
    IF `prescribed as excluded`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `at a workplace` AND `serious risk` AND `a listed exposure`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `a listed exposure` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the exposure`
            WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 35: "notifiable incident means-- (a) the death of a person; or (b) a serious injury or illness of a person; or (c) a
-- dangerous incident." "means" -- JUST FALSE when none.
GIVEN `a death` IS A BOOLEAN, `serious injury or illness` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, `dangerous incident` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35 -- notifiable incident` `a death` `serious injury or illness` `dangerous incident` MEANS
    IF `a death` OR `serious injury or illness` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `dangerous incident` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 38(1): "A person who conducts a business or undertaking must ensure that the regulator is notified immediately after
-- becoming aware that a notifiable incident arising out of the conduct of the business or undertaking has occurred."
-- A duty whose "that ... arising out of" condition is unmet: the Act puts no duty to notify on the business -- JUST FALSE
-- (fork F4). Not a notifiable incident: JUST FALSE (s 35 is a "means" definition).
GIVEN `notifiable` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, `arising out of the business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38(1) -- the business must notify the regulator` `notifiable` `arising out of the business` MEANS
    IF `notifiable` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `arising out of the business`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 38(7): the business "must keep a record of each notifiable incident for at least 5 years from the day that notice of
-- the incident is given to the regulator". The record may be destroyed after the day 5 years on (fork F1).
GIVEN `the notice day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 38(7) -- the record must be kept until` `the notice day` MEANS `the day` 5 `years after` `the notice day`

-- s 39(3): actions the duty to preserve the site does not prevent.
DECLARE `Action at the site` IS ONE OF
    `to assist an injured person`
    `to remove a deceased person`
    `essential to make the site safe or to minimise the risk of a further notifiable incident`
    `associated with a police investigation`
    `permitted by an inspector or the regulator`
    `any other action`

-- s 39(1): the person with management or control of the workplace "must ensure so far as is reasonably practicable, that
-- the site where the incident occurred is not disturbed until an inspector arrives at the site or any earlier time that
-- an inspector directs"; (3) "Subsection (1) does not prevent any action" (a)-(e).
-- JUST TRUE: the duty forbids this action. JUST FALSE: "until" has passed, or "does not prevent" (a flat negative).
-- NOTHING: not a notifiable incident, so s 39 does not reach it (NOTHING-kind: limits a prohibition in its own wording).
-- "so far as is reasonably practicable" is a judgment for others and does not change which actions are reached.
GIVEN `notifiable` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, `an inspector has arrived or released the site` IS A BOOLEAN, `the action` IS AN `Action at the site`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39 -- the site must not be disturbed by the action` `notifiable` `an inspector has arrived or released the site` `the action` MEANS
    IF NOT (`notifiable` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `an inspector has arrived or released the site`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE CONSIDER `the action`
              WHEN `any other action` THEN JUST TRUE
              OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 5 Division 6 -- the right to cease unsafe work`

DECLARE `How I ceased work` IS ONE OF
    `on my own concern (s 84)`
    `on a direction from a health and safety representative (s 85)`
    `I have not ceased work under the division`

-- s 84: "A worker may cease, or refuse to carry out, work if the worker has a reasonable concern that to carry out the
-- work would expose the worker to a serious risk to the worker's health or safety, emanating from an immediate or
-- imminent exposure to a hazard." "if" -- JUST FALSE when the condition fails. Whether the concern is reasonable is
-- asked as an input: a tribunal's judgment, not this encoding's.
GIVEN `worker` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, `concern` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN, `serious risk to me` IS A BOOLEAN, `immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84 -- I may cease or refuse to carry out the work` `worker` `concern` `reasonable` `serious risk to me` `immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard` MEANS
    CONSIDER `worker`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `concern` AND `reasonable` AND `serious risk to me` AND `immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind: leaves a term undefined (whether there is a business or undertaking).
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 86(a): a worker who ceases work under the division must "as soon as practicable, notify the person conducting the
-- business or undertaking that the worker has ceased work under this division unless the worker ceased work under a
-- direction from a health and safety representative". "unless" -- JUST FALSE when it is met.
-- Not having ceased work under the division: the duty's "who ceases work" condition is unmet -- JUST FALSE (fork F4).
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I ceased work`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86(a) -- I must notify the business that I have ceased work` `how` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `on my own concern (s 84)` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 86(b): the worker must "remain available to carry out suitable alternative work".
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I ceased work`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86(b) -- I must remain available for suitable alternative work` `how` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `I have not ceased work under the division` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 87: the business "may direct the worker to carry out suitable alternative work at the same or another workplace if
-- that work is safe and appropriate for the worker to carry out until the worker can resume normal duties". "if" and
-- "until" -- JUST FALSE when either fails.
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I ceased work`, `suitable` IS A BOOLEAN, `safe and appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN, `I can resume normal duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87 -- the business may direct me to alternative work` `how` `suitable` `safe and appropriate` `I can resume normal duties` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `I have not ceased work under the division` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        IF `suitable` AND `safe and appropriate` AND (NOT `I can resume normal duties`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 88: ceasing work "does not affect the continuity of engagement of the worker for prescribed purposes if the worker
-- has not unreasonably failed to comply with a direction to carry out suitable alternative work-- (a) at the same or
-- another workplace; and (b) that was safe and appropriate for the worker to carry out." The prescribed purposes are in
-- a regulation (not deposited). JUST TRUE: protected. Where the worker unreasonably failed to follow such a direction,
-- the Act does not say the continuity IS affected; it only withdraws its protection -- NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: is silent).
-- A failure to follow a direction to work that was not safe and appropriate is not within the "if" at all: protected.
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I ceased work`, `a direction to alternative work was given` IS A BOOLEAN, `the work was suitable, safe and appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN, `I unreasonably failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 88 -- my continuity of engagement is protected` `how` `a direction to alternative work was given` `the work was suitable, safe and appropriate` `I unreasonably failed to comply` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how`
    -- NOTHING-kind: limits a grant in its own wording (only work ceased under the division).
    WHEN `I have not ceased work under the division` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        IF `a direction to alternative work was given` AND `the work was suitable, safe and appropriate` AND `I unreasonably failed to comply`
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part 6 -- discriminatory, coercive and misleading conduct`

-- s 105: what was done (to a worker, a prospective worker, or another person in a commercial arrangement).
DECLARE `What was done` IS ONE OF
    `dismissed me`
    `terminated my contract for services`
    `put me to my detriment in my engagement`
    `altered my position to my detriment`
    `treated me less favourably than other workers`
    `refused or failed to offer to engage me as a prospective worker`
    `treated me less favourably than another prospective worker in offering terms of engagement`
    `terminated a commercial arrangement with me`
    `refused or failed to enter into a commercial arrangement with me`
    `something else`

-- s 105(1), (2): "a person engages in discriminatory conduct if" one of the acts in (1), or "organises to take any
-- action mentioned in subsection (1) or threatens to organise or take that action". "if" -- JUST FALSE for anything else.
-- `whether done or only organised or threatened` is not an input: (2) makes the three the same.
GIVEN `the act` IS A `What was done`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 -- discriminatory conduct` `the act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `something else` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 106: the prohibited reasons, (a) to (j). Each covers the past, the present and a proposal ("is, has been or
-- proposes to be").
DECLARE `Reason` IS ONE OF
    `being a work health and safety officer, health and safety representative or committee member`
    `undertaking another role under the Act`
    `exercising a power or performing a function as such an officer, representative or member`
    `exercising a power under the Act, or in a particular way`
    `performing a function under the Act, or in a particular way`
    `refraining from exercising a power or performing a function under the Act`
    `assisting or giving information to a person exercising a power or performing a function under the Act`
    `raising an issue or concern about work health and safety with a listed person`
    `being involved in resolving a work health and safety issue under the Act`
    `taking action to seek compliance with a duty or obligation under the Act`
    `another reason`

-- s 106: conduct "is engaged in for a prohibited reason if it is engaged in because" of (a)-(j). The listed persons in
-- (h) are the business, an inspector, an entry permit holder, a health and safety representative, a work health and
-- safety officer other than the business, a committee member, another worker, another duty holder, or another person
-- exercising a power or function under the Act; together they cover nearly anyone with a role, so they are one choice.
-- "if" -- JUST FALSE for another reason.
GIVEN `the reason` IS A `Reason`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106 -- a prohibited reason` `the reason` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    WHEN `another reason` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 108(1)(a)-(d): what the coercion or inducement aimed at.
DECLARE `Aim of the action` IS ONE OF
    `to make me exercise, or not exercise, a power under the Act`
    `to make me perform, or not perform, a function under the Act`
    `to make me exercise a power or perform a function in a particular way`
    `to make me refrain from seeking, or continuing to undertake, a role under the Act`
    `another aim`

-- s 108(1): "A person must not organise or take, or threaten to organise or take, any action against another person
-- with intent to coerce or induce the other person, or a third person" to do (a)-(d), proposals included. (2): action
-- includes not taking an action. (3): "a reasonable direction given by an emergency services worker in an emergency is
-- not an action with intent to coerce or induce a person." JUST TRUE: prohibited. JUST FALSE: (3) applies (a flat
-- negative), or no intent to coerce or induce (the prohibition's own "with intent" -- fork F5), or another aim.
GIVEN `action taken or threatened` IS A BOOLEAN, `intent to coerce or induce` IS A BOOLEAN, `the aim` IS AN `Aim of the action`, `a reasonable emergency direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108 -- prohibited coercion or inducement` `action taken or threatened` `intent to coerce or induce` `the aim` `a reasonable emergency direction` MEANS
    IF `a reasonable emergency direction`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `action taken or threatened` AND `intent to coerce or induce` AND `a listed aim`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `a listed aim` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the aim`
            WHEN `another aim` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 109(1)(a)-(c): what the representation was about.
DECLARE `Subject of the representation` IS ONE OF
    `my rights or obligations under the Act`
    `my ability to initiate, or participate in, a process or proceedings under the Act`
    `my ability to complain or inquire to a person or body that seeks compliance with the Act`
    `something else`

-- s 109: "A person must not knowingly or recklessly make a false or misleading representation to another person about
-- that other person's" (a)-(c). (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the person to whom the representation is made
-- would not be expected to rely on it." JUST FALSE: (2) applies, or the representation falls outside (1)'s own terms
-- (fork F5).
GIVEN `false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN, `knowingly or recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN, `the subject` IS A `Subject of the representation`, `I would be expected to rely on it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109 -- prohibited misrepresentation` `false or misleading` `knowingly or recklessly` `the subject` `I would be expected to rely on it` MEANS
    IF NOT `I would be expected to rely on it`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `false or misleading` AND `knowingly or recklessly` AND `a listed subject`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `a listed subject` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the subject`
            WHEN `something else` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 112(2): the conduct a civil application can be about.
DECLARE `Conduct complained of` IS ONE OF
    `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason (s 112(2)(a))`
    `requesting, instructing, inducing, encouraging, authorising or assisting another to engage in it (s 112(2)(b))`
    `coercion or inducement contravening s 108 (s 112(2)(c))`
    `misrepresentation contravening s 109`

-- s 112(6): "each of the following is an eligible person-- (a) a person affected by the contravention; (b) if a worker is
-- affected by the contravention as a worker-- a suitable entity representing the worker; (c) if a person is affected by
-- the contravention other than as a worker-- someone who is authorised as a representative by the person." The seat
-- is the person affected, so (a) is the one asked; (b) and (c) are in the description.
DECLARE `Who is applying` IS ONE OF
    `I am the person affected`
    `a suitable entity representing me, affected as a worker`
    `a representative I have authorised, affected other than as a worker`
    `someone else`

-- s 112(1), (6): "An eligible person may apply to the commission". Eligibility is a closed list ("each of the following
-- is"), read as JUST FALSE for someone else (fork F6). s 109 misrepresentation is not in s 112(2): JUST FALSE (s 112(2)
-- lists what the commission may make orders about; finding 2).
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `Conduct complained of`, `the applicant` IS A `Who is applying`, `I am affected as a worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 112(1), (6) -- the applicant may apply to the commission` `the conduct` `the applicant` `I am affected as a worker` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `misrepresentation contravening s 109` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the applicant`
        WHEN `I am the person affected` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a suitable entity representing me, affected as a worker` THEN
            IF `I am affected as a worker` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
        WHEN `a representative I have authorised, affected other than as a worker` THEN
            IF `I am affected as a worker` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 112(4) with s 113(2), (4): the commission may find discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason "only if a reason
-- mentioned in section 106 was a substantial reason for the conduct"; if a prohibited reason is alleged, "that reason is
-- presumed to be a substantial reason ... unless the defendant proves, on the balance of probabilities, that the reason
-- was not a substantial reason". "only if" and "unless" -- JUST FALSE when the defendant has proved it.
-- For s 112(2)(c) (coercion) the question does not arise; the s 108 answer decides.
GIVEN `discriminatory` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, `prohibited reason alleged` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, `the other side proved it was not a substantial reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 112(4), 113(2) -- discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason can be found` `discriminatory` `prohibited reason alleged` `the other side proved it was not a substantial reason` MEANS
    IF `discriminatory` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `prohibited reason alleged` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (NOT `the other side proved it was not a substantial reason`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 113(3): "It is a defence to a proceeding under section 112 in relation to conduct mentioned in section 112(2)(a) or (b)
-- if the defendant proves that-- (a) the conduct was reasonable in the circumstances; and (b) a substantial reason for
-- the conduct was to comply with the requirements of this Act or a corresponding WHS law." By the ruling of 2026-11-05
-- (b): when not proved, JUST FALSE ("this section gives no defence on these facts"). For s 112(2)(c) the section gives
-- no defence at all: JUST FALSE likewise, worded in the seat.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `Conduct complained of`, `proved reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved substantial reason was compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(3) -- the other side has a defence` `the conduct` `proved reasonable` `proved substantial reason was compliance` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason (s 112(2)(a))` THEN `proved both`
    WHEN `requesting, instructing, inducing, encouraging, authorising or assisting another to engage in it (s 112(2)(b))` THEN `proved both`
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `proved both` MEANS
            IF `proved reasonable` AND `proved substantial reason was compliance`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The orders, s 111 and s 112(3).
DECLARE `Order` IS ONE OF
    `an injunction`
    `compensation paid to me within a stated period`
    `reinstatement or re-employment in my former or a similar position`
    `employment in the position I applied for or a similar position`
    `any other order the commission considers appropriate`

-- What happened in other proceedings about the same matter, for s 114(2), (3) and s 115.
DECLARE `Other proceedings` HAS
    `a court made a s 111 order for the same conduct`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `another proceeding of mine on the same matter is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I received compensation for the matter under another law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I failed in another proceeding on the same matter`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `that proceeding was about workers' compensation`          IS A BOOLEAN

`no other proceedings` MEANS
    `Other proceedings` WITH
        `a court made a s 111 order for the same conduct`        IS FALSE
        `another proceeding of mine on the same matter is pending` IS FALSE
        `I received compensation for the matter under another law` IS FALSE
        `I failed in another proceeding on the same matter`        IS FALSE
        `that proceeding was about workers' compensation`          IS FALSE

-- s 115(a), (c): "A person can not-- (a) commence a proceeding under division 3 if the person has commenced a proceeding
-- or made an application or complaint in relation to the same matter under a law of the Commonwealth or a State and that
-- proceeding, application or complaint has not been withdrawn; ... (c) commence or continue an application under
-- division 3 if the person has failed in a proceeding, application or complaint in relation to the same matter under a
-- law of the Commonwealth or a State, other than a proceeding, application or complaint relating to workers'
-- compensation." JUST TRUE: barred. JUST FALSE: neither bar applies ("can not ... if" -- the "if" fails).
GIVEN o IS AN `Other proceedings`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(a), (c) -- I am barred from applying` o MEANS
    IF o's `another proceeding of mine on the same matter is pending`
       OR (o's `I failed in another proceeding on the same matter` AND (NOT (o's `that proceeding was about workers' compensation`)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 112(3), s 114(3), s 115(b): the orders the commission may make for the person who was the subject of the conduct.
-- (a) an injunction: for any conduct in s 112(2); (b) compensation: only for (2)(a) or (b); (c) reinstatement,
-- re-employment or employment: only for (2)(a), "in relation to a worker who was or is an employee or prospective
-- employee"; (d) any other order. s 114(3): if a court made a s 111 order for the same conduct, the commission "can not
-- make an order under section 112" for (2)(a) or (b) conduct: no orders. s 115(b): "can not ... recover any compensation
-- under division 3 if the person has received compensation for the matter" under another law. An empty list: none.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `Conduct complained of`, `employee or prospective employee` IS A BOOLEAN, `I applied for a position` IS A BOOLEAN, o IS AN `Other proceedings`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Order`
`s 112(3) -- the orders the commission may make for me` `the conduct` `employee or prospective employee` `I applied for a position` o MEANS
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `misrepresentation contravening s 109` THEN EMPTY
    WHEN `coercion or inducement contravening s 108 (s 112(2)(c))` THEN LIST `an injunction`, `any other order the commission considers appropriate`
    WHEN `requesting, instructing, inducing, encouraging, authorising or assisting another to engage in it (s 112(2)(b))` THEN
        IF o's `a court made a s 111 order for the same conduct`
        THEN EMPTY
        ELSE IF o's `I received compensation for the matter under another law`
             THEN LIST `an injunction`, `any other order the commission considers appropriate`
             ELSE LIST `an injunction`, `compensation paid to me within a stated period`, `any other order the commission considers appropriate`
    WHEN `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason (s 112(2)(a))` THEN
        IF o's `a court made a s 111 order for the same conduct`
        THEN EMPTY
        ELSE `the orders` `the injunction` `then` (`the orders` `the compensation` `then` (`the orders` `the position` `then` `the other order`))
    WHERE
        `the injunction` MEANS LIST `an injunction`
        `the compensation` MEANS
            IF o's `I received compensation for the matter under another law`
            THEN EMPTY
            ELSE LIST `compensation paid to me within a stated period`
        `the position` MEANS
            IF `employee or prospective employee`
            THEN IF `I applied for a position`
                 THEN LIST `employment in the position I applied for or a similar position`
                 ELSE LIST `reinstatement or re-employment in my former or a similar position`
            ELSE EMPTY
        `the other order` MEANS LIST `any other order the commission considers appropriate`

GIVEN a IS A LIST OF `Order`
      b IS A LIST OF `Order`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Order`
`the orders` a `then` b MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN EMPTY THEN b
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN x FOLLOWED BY (`the orders` rest `then` b)

-- s 111: "If a person is convicted or found guilty of an offence against section 104 or 107, the court may (in addition
-- to imposing a penalty) make either or both of" (a) compensation to the person who was the subject of the discriminatory
-- conduct; (b) for an employee or prospective employee, reinstatement or re-employment, or employment in the position
-- applied for. s 114(2): if the commission made a s 112 order for the same conduct, "a court can not make an order under
-- section 111". Not convicted: the "If" fails -- empty.
GIVEN `convicted of an offence against s 104 or 107` IS A BOOLEAN, `employee or prospective employee` IS A BOOLEAN, `I applied for a position` IS A BOOLEAN, `the commission made a s 112 order for the same conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Order`
`s 111 -- the orders the court may make for me` `convicted of an offence against s 104 or 107` `employee or prospective employee` `I applied for a position` `the commission made a s 112 order for the same conduct` MEANS
    IF `convicted of an offence against s 104 or 107` AND (NOT `the commission made a s 112 order for the same conduct`)
    THEN `the orders` (LIST `compensation paid to me within a stated period`) `then` `the position`
    ELSE EMPTY
    WHERE
        `the position` MEANS
            IF `employee or prospective employee`
            THEN IF `I applied for a position`
                 THEN LIST `employment in the position I applied for or a similar position`
                 ELSE LIST `reinstatement or re-employment in my former or a similar position`
            ELSE EMPTY

-- s 113(1): "A proceeding taken under section 112 must be commenced not more than 1 year after the date on which the
-- applicant knew or ought to have known that the cause of action accrued." The last day is the anniversary (fork F1).
-- Whether the applicant "ought to have known" earlier is a judgment, so the day is an input.
GIVEN `the day I knew or ought to have known` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 113(1) -- the last day to commence` `the day I knew or ought to have known` MEANS `the day` 1 `years after` `the day I knew or ought to have known`

§§ `s 184 -- compensation for the exercise of entry powers`

-- s 184(1): "A person may claim compensation from the State if the person incurs loss or expense because of the exercise
-- or purported exercise of a power under division 3" (the inspectors' powers relating to entry). (3): "The court may
-- order compensation to be paid only if it is satisfied it is just to make the order". The first answer is whether I may
-- claim; the second whether the court may order it.
GIVEN `loss or expense` IS A BOOLEAN, `because of a power of entry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(1) -- I may claim compensation from the State` `loss or expense` `because of a power of entry` MEANS
    IF `loss or expense` AND `because of a power of entry`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `may claim` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, `the court is satisfied it is just` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(3) -- the court may order compensation` `may claim` `the court is satisfied it is just` MEANS
    IF `may claim` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the court is satisfied it is just`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 12 -- review of decisions`

-- Schedule 2A, items 4 to 13.
DECLARE `Decision` IS ONE OF
    `s 102 decision on review of a provisional improvement notice (item 4)`
    `s 179 forfeiture of a thing (item 5)`
    `s 180 return of seized things (item 6)`
    `s 191 issue of an improvement notice (item 7)`
    `s 194 extension of time to comply with an improvement notice (item 8)`
    `s 195 issue of a prohibition notice (item 9)`
    `s 198 issue of a non-disturbance notice (item 10)`
    `s 201 issue of a subsequent notice (item 11)`
    `s 207 regulator's decision to vary or cancel a notice (item 12)`
    `a decision under a provision prescribed by regulation (item 13)`

-- s 223(1)(b), schedule 2A: who is an eligible person. For a worker, items 4 and 7 to 12 name "A worker whose interests
-- are affected by the decision"; items 5 and 6 name only "The person entitled to the thing"; items 4 and 7 to 12 also
-- name the person to whom the notice was issued. Item 13 is left to a regulation (not deposited): NOTHING (NOTHING-kind:
-- points outside the sources). Otherwise the schedule "states ... who is eligible": JUST FALSE for anyone else (fork F6).
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Decision`, `my interests as a worker are affected` IS A BOOLEAN, `the notice was issued to me` IS A BOOLEAN, `I am the person entitled to the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`schedule 2A -- I am an eligible person` `the decision` `my interests as a worker are affected` `the notice was issued to me` `I am the person entitled to the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a decision under a provision prescribed by regulation (item 13)` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `s 179 forfeiture of a thing (item 5)` THEN `entitled`
    WHEN `s 180 return of seized things (item 6)` THEN `entitled`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `my interests as a worker are affected` OR `the notice was issued to me`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `entitled` MEANS IF `I am the person entitled to the thing` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Review step` IS ONE OF
    `apply for internal review by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `no internal review: apply to the commission for external review by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the period is set by a regulation and the QCAT Act`

-- s 224(1), (3): an eligible person "in relation to a reviewable decision, other than a decision made by the regulator or
-- a delegate of the regulator, may apply to the regulator for review ... within-- (a) the prescribed time after the day
-- on which the decision first came to the eligible person's notice; or (b) the longer period the regulator allows." The
-- prescribed time is, for a decision to issue an improvement notice, "the period stated in the notice for compliance
-- with the notice or 14 days, whichever is the lesser", and otherwise 14 days. A decision of the regulator or its
-- delegate goes straight to external review (s 229(1)(a)): for the commission, within 30 days after the day it first
-- came to the applicant's notice (s 229B(2)). Item 13 decisions are for a regulation and possibly QCAT.
-- The regulator's longer period, if allowed, is an input (0 if none).
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Decision`, `made by the regulator or a delegate` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day it came to my notice` IS A DATE, `the compliance period in days` IS A NUMBER, `the longer period the regulator allowed in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Review step`
`s 224 -- my first review step` `the decision` `made by the regulator or a delegate` `the day it came to my notice` `the compliance period in days` `the longer period the regulator allowed in days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a decision under a provision prescribed by regulation (item 13)` THEN `the period is set by a regulation and the QCAT Act`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `made by the regulator or a delegate`
        THEN `no internal review: apply to the commission for external review by` (`s 229B(2) -- the last day to file` `the day it came to my notice`)
        ELSE `apply for internal review by` (`the day` (max `the prescribed time` `the longer period the regulator allowed in days`) `days after` `the day it came to my notice`)
    WHERE
        `the prescribed time` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the decision`
            WHEN `s 191 issue of an improvement notice (item 7)` THEN min `the compliance period in days` 14
            OTHERWISE 14

-- s 229B(2), (3): "The application for a review must be filed within 30 days after the day on which the decision first
-- came to the applicant's notice"; the commission "may at any time extend the period".
GIVEN `the day it came to my notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 229B(2) -- the last day to file` `the day it came to my notice` MEANS `the day` 30 `days after` `the day it came to my notice`

-- s 226(1), (3), (6): the internal reviewer must decide "within 14 days after the application for internal review is
-- received"; if the reviewer seeks further information "the 14-day period ceases to run until the applicant provides the
-- information"; "If the reviewable decision is not varied or set aside within the 14-day period, the decision is taken to
-- have been confirmed". (5): if the applicant does not give the information within the time stated (at least 7 days),
-- the decision "is taken to have been confirmed ... at the end of that time".
GIVEN `the day received` IS A DATE, `days paused for information` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 226(6) -- the day my decision is taken to be confirmed` `the day received` `days paused for information` MEANS
    `the day` (14 PLUS `days paused for information`) `days after` `the day received`

-- s 228(1)-(5): an application for internal review "stays the operation of the decision", other than a decision to issue
-- a prohibition notice or a non-disturbance notice; for those, "the reviewer may stay" it, must decide an application
-- for a stay "within 1 working day", and if it has not, "is taken to have made a decision to grant a stay".
DECLARE `Stay request` IS ONE OF
    `I did not apply for a stay`
    `the reviewer granted a stay`
    `the reviewer refused within 1 working day`
    `the reviewer did not decide within 1 working day`

-- JUST TRUE: stayed. JUST FALSE: a prohibition or non-disturbance notice and no stay granted or taken to be granted (the
-- "other than" carves those out of (1), and (2) makes a stay the reviewer's decision -- fork F7).
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Decision`, `the stay` IS A `Stay request`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 228 -- my internal review application stays the decision` `the decision` `the stay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `s 195 issue of a prohibition notice (item 9)` THEN `on the reviewer`
    WHEN `s 198 issue of a non-disturbance notice (item 10)` THEN `on the reviewer`
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `on the reviewer` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the stay`
            WHEN `the reviewer granted a stay` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `the reviewer did not decide within 1 working day` THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 231, 232 -- asking for a prosecution, and the time to bring one`

DECLARE `Why I consider an offence was committed` IS ONE OF
    `I reasonably consider the act or omission is a category 1 or category 2 offence`
    `I reasonably consider the act or omission is an industrial manslaughter offence (Part 2A)`
    `a coronial report or inquest shows me it is a category 1 or category 2 offence`
    `none of these`

-- s 231(1), (1A), (1B): the applicant "may make a written request to the WHS prosecutor that a prosecution be brought"
-- if they reasonably consider (i) a category 1 or 2 offence, (ii) a Part 2A offence, or (iii) from a coronial report or
-- inquest, a category 1 or 2 offence, and "no prosecution has been brought". "However, the request may only be made if--
-- (a) if subsection (1)(a)(i) applies-- it has been at least 6 months but not more than 18 months since the act or
-- omission happened; or (b) if subsection (1)(a)(ii) applies-- it has been at least 6 months since the act or omission
-- happened; or (c) if subsection (1)(a)(iii) applies-- it has been not more than 6 months since the report was made or
-- the inquiry or inquest ended." "only if" -- JUST FALSE outside the window. The window counts in months from the day
-- (fork F1): open from the day 6 months on, closed after the day 18 months on.
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Why I consider an offence was committed`, `a prosecution has been brought` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE, `the day of the report or the end of the inquest` IS A DATE, `the day of my request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(1B) -- I may request a prosecution` `the ground` `a prosecution has been brought` `the day of the act or omission` `the day of the report or the end of the inquest` `the day of my request` MEANS
    IF `a prosecution has been brought`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the ground`
         WHEN `I reasonably consider the act or omission is a category 1 or category 2 offence` THEN
             `yes or no` (`6 months have passed since the act` AND (NOT (`the day of my request` `falls after` (`the day` 18 `months after` `the day of the act or omission`))))
         WHEN `I reasonably consider the act or omission is an industrial manslaughter offence (Part 2A)` THEN
             `yes or no` `6 months have passed since the act`
         WHEN `a coronial report or inquest shows me it is a category 1 or category 2 offence` THEN
             `yes or no` ((NOT (`the day of my request` `falls before` `the day of the report or the end of the inquest`)) AND (NOT (`the day of my request` `falls after` (`the day` 6 `months after` `the day of the report or the end of the inquest`))))
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `6 months have passed since the act` MEANS NOT (`the day of my request` `falls before` (`the day` 6 `months after` `the day of the act or omission`))

GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`yes or no` b MEANS IF b THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 231(2): "Within 3 months after the WHS prosecutor receives a request under subsection (1A) the WHS prosecutor must--
-- (a) advise the applicant, in writing-- (i) whether the investigation is complete; and (ii) if the investigation is
-- complete, whether a prosecution has been or will be brought or give reasons why a prosecution will not be brought".
GIVEN `the day the request was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 231(2) -- the WHS prosecutor must advise me by` `the day the request was received` MEANS `the day` 3 `months after` `the day the request was received`

-- s 231(3)(b): if told a prosecution for a category 1 or 2 or Part 2A offence will not be brought, the applicant may ask
-- in writing for a referral to the director of public prosecutions; the WHS prosecutor must "refer the matter to the
-- director of public prosecutions within 1 month of the request". (4): the director "must consider the matter and
-- advise (in writing) the WHS prosecutor within 1 month"; read as 1 month from the referral (fork F8).
GIVEN `the day of my request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 231(3)(b) -- the matter must be referred to the DPP by` `the day of my request` MEANS `the day` 1 `months after` `the day of my request`

GIVEN `the day of the referral` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 231(4) -- the DPP must advise by` `the day of the referral` MEANS `the day` 1 `months after` `the day of the referral`

DECLARE `Prosecution time limit` IS ONE OF
    `no limitation period (industrial manslaughter, s 232(3))`
    `proceedings may be taken until` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the limitation period has ended, but fresh evidence lets a category 1 prosecution proceed (s 232(2))` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

-- s 232(1): "Proceedings for an offence against this Act may be taken within the latest of the following periods-- (a)
-- within 2 years after the offence first comes to the notice of the WHS prosecutor; (b) within 1 year after a coronial
-- report was made or a coronial inquiry or inquest ended, if it appeared from the report or the proceedings ... that an
-- offence had been committed against this Act; (c) if a WHS undertaking has been given in relation to the offence,
-- within 6 months after-- (i) the WHS undertaking is contravened; or (ii) it comes to the notice of the regulator that
-- the WHS undertaking has been contravened; or (iii) the regulator has agreed under section 221 to the withdrawal of the
-- WHS undertaking." (2): a category 1 offence may be prosecuted after the period if fresh evidence is discovered and the
-- court is satisfied it could not reasonably have been discovered within it. (3): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a
-- proceeding for an offence against part 2A."
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`, `the day it came to the WHS prosecutor's notice` IS A DATE, `a coronial finding` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day of the coronial report or end of the inquest` IS A DATE, `an undertaking event` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day of the undertaking event` IS A DATE, `the court accepts fresh evidence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Prosecution time limit`
`s 232 -- the time to prosecute` `the offence` `the day it came to the WHS prosecutor's notice` `a coronial finding` `the day of the coronial report or end of the inquest` `an undertaking event` `the day of the undertaking event` `the court accepts fresh evidence` `the day asked about` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `industrial manslaughter by the person conducting the business or undertaking` THEN `no limitation period (industrial manslaughter, s 232(3))`
    WHEN `industrial manslaughter by a senior officer` THEN `no limitation period (industrial manslaughter, s 232(3))`
    WHEN `category 1 -- reckless or negligent conduct exposing me to a risk of death or serious injury or illness` THEN
        IF `the court accepts fresh evidence` AND `the day asked about` `falls after` `the last day`
        THEN `the limitation period has ended, but fresh evidence lets a category 1 prosecution proceed (s 232(2))` `the last day`
        ELSE `proceedings may be taken until` `the last day`
    OTHERWISE `proceedings may be taken until` `the last day`
    WHERE
        `the 2-year day` MEANS `the day` 2 `years after` `the day it came to the WHS prosecutor's notice`
        `with the coronial day` MEANS
            IF `a coronial finding`
            THEN `the later day of` `the 2-year day` `and` (`the day` 1 `years after` `the day of the coronial report or end of the inquest`)
            ELSE `the 2-year day`
        `the last day` MEANS
            IF `an undertaking event`
            THEN `the later day of` `with the coronial day` `and` (`the day` 6 `months after` `the day of the undertaking event`)
            ELSE `with the coronial day`

§§ `s 267, s 272, s 273 -- civil liability, contracting out, levies`

DECLARE `What my claim rests on` IS ONE OF
    `discriminatory or coercive conduct (Part 6)`
    `a breach of a health and safety duty or another provision of the Act`
    `a breach of a duty under a regulation`
    `a WHS civil penalty provision or the entry permit provisions (Part 5 Division 7A, Part 7)`

-- s 267: "Except as provided in part 6 and part 7 and division 7, nothing in this Act is to be construed as-- (a)
-- conferring a right of action in civil proceedings in relation to a contravention of a provision of this Act; or (b)
-- conferring a defence to an action in civil proceedings or otherwise affecting a right of action in civil proceedings;
-- or (c) affecting the extent (if any) to which a right of action arises ... in relation to breaches of duties or
-- obligations imposed under a regulation." JUST TRUE: Part 6 gives civil proceedings (s 112). JUST FALSE: the Act gives
-- no civil right of action (a flat negative). NOTHING: a regulation's duty ((c) leaves it to the general law), and the
-- civil penalty and entry provisions, which are outside this encoding (NOTHING-kind: points outside the sources).
GIVEN `the basis` IS A `What my claim rests on`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 267 -- the Act gives me a civil right of action` `the basis` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the basis`
    WHEN `discriminatory or coercive conduct (Part 6)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a breach of a health and safety duty or another provision of the Act` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 272: "A term of any agreement or contract that purports to exclude, limit or modify the operation of this Act or any
-- duty owed under this Act or to transfer to another person any duty owed under this Act is void." JUST TRUE: void.
-- NOTHING for any other term (NOTHING-kind: is silent).
GIVEN `excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty` IS A BOOLEAN, `transfers a duty to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272 -- the term is void` `excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty` `transfers a duty to another person` MEANS
    IF `excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty` OR `transfers a duty to another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 273: "A person conducting a business or undertaking must not impose a levy or charge on a worker, or permit a levy or
-- charge to be imposed on a worker, for anything done, or provided, in relation to work health and safety." By ruling N2,
-- the flat negative is the answer: may the business charge me? JUST FALSE. Outside the prohibition (not its worker, or
-- not for work health and safety): NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: limits a prohibition in its own wording).
GIVEN `I am its worker` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, `for work health and safety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273 -- the business may charge me` `I am its worker` `for work health and safety` MEANS
    IF `I am its worker` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `for work health and safety`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Time limits as regulative rules`

-- The deadlines, as rules over a day-numbered timeline starting at 0. FULFILLED means the step was taken in time. They
-- take DEONTIC values, so they are never exported; the seat questions run them by EVALTRACE on plain dates.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant`
    `the WHS prosecutor`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `commence the proceeding`
    `apply for review`
    `advise the applicant in writing`

-- s 113(1), s 224(1), s 229B(2): what I must do to keep my claim or review.
GIVEN `the step` IS A `Step`, `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`I must take` `the step` `within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST EXACTLY `the step`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "the time the Act allows has run out, unless the commission or the regulator extends it where the Act lets it (ss 224(1)(b), 229B(3))"

-- s 231(2): what the WHS prosecutor must do once my request is received.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the WHS prosecutor must advise me within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the WHS prosecutor`
    MUST `advise the applicant in writing`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the WHS prosecutor` BECAUSE "the WHS prosecutor did not advise the applicant within 3 months after receiving the request (s 231(2))"

GIVEN `the step` IS A `Step`, `the party` IS A `Party`, `the time of the step` IS A NUMBER, `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `taking` `the step` `by` `the party` `at` `the time of the step` `satisfies` `the rule` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time of the step`), (EVENT `the party` `the step` `the time of the step`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Whether a step taken on a day meets a deadline that ends on a last day. The timeline starts at the earlier of the two
-- days, so a step before the start is in time.
GIVEN `the step` IS A `Step`, `the party` IS A `Party`, `the day of the step` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the step` `by` `the party` `on` `the day of the step` `is in time for` `the last day` IF
    `taking` `the step` `by` `the party` `at` (`the number of days from` `the base` `to` `the day of the step`) `satisfies` `the rule`
    WHERE
        `the base` MEANS `the earlier day of` `the day of the step` `and` `the last day`
        `the allowed` MEANS `the number of days from` `the base` `to` `the last day`
        `the rule` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the party`
            WHEN `the WHS prosecutor` THEN `the WHS prosecutor must advise me within` `the allowed`
            OTHERWISE `I must take` `the step` `within` `the allowed`
